In article <2401@taux01.UUCP> crehta@taux01.nsc.com (Ran Ever-Hadani) writes:

[ ... ]

>A partial solution is enclosing every appearance of $PAGER in double
>quotes.   But when $PATH is searched for $PAGER, the search will fail
>and $PAGER will be unset.  I don't know how you can extract the 'less'
>from 'less -sm' to solve that.  Any ideas?

Sure.  RT*M page for less(1).  You can pass options to less with the
LESS enviroment variable.  So, in (for example) your .profile, put:

  LESS="-sm"
  export LESS

and change your PAGER to just "less".

